From 20deaa3ccf306e47e1b34ebe7f6f64e12eae7ea1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harbor_agent): chisel and OpenCode from binaries the
 sandbox platform mounts

The sandbox platform can mount the agent binaries into every pod (on Breithorn: read-only image
volumes under /opt/rl-tools/<name>/<version>/). Then nothing has to be uploaded per sandbox:

- model_tunnel.pod_install: mounted uses chisel at pod_binary as it is. No upload, no chmod (the
  mount is read-only), the server log goes to /tmp/.nemo-gym-chisel.log (pod_log), and chisel_dir
  needs only the node's binary (the client runs on the node: the node's architecture, e.g. arm64 on
  GH200, while the sandbox's chisel is amd64). Only a missing binary fails the start.
- opencode_install: mounted with opencode_bin: setup runs a check script instead of an install
  (only a missing or non-executable binary fails agent setup, failure class infra as for a failed
  install), and the run calls the binary by that path.

No version is required of a mounted binary; its --version (bounded by timeout 10 where the image
has it) is logged: for chisel in the tunnel's "up" line (both install modes), for the agent in
setup/stdout.txt and the agent's logger. installed_compat.check_mounted_binary holds the check for
any adapter. upload stays the default for both.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
